# vercel.json sets "outputDirectory": ".", which makes the repo root the web
# root — anything deployed here is publicly served. So ignore the root by
# default and allow only what the site serves or the build needs. New internal
# files (notes, docs, plans) then stay private without anyone remembering to
# add them here.
/*

!*.html
!script.js
!styles.css
!web-subscribe.js
!art-first.js
!art-first.css
!assets
!data
!lang

# Vercel builds api/ into functions and never serves it statically, which is
# why the server-only helpers live in api/_lib rather than at the root: they
# cannot be excluded here, because functions need them at build time.
!api

# Needed to install function dependencies. Vercel keeps these out of the
# static output on its own.
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!vercel.json
